body:
Agreed on the mechanics, and this limitation is called out in the PR description: `add_to_platform_start` pins the previously registered unit for entities that already exist, so only new registrations pick up the suggestion.

I'd argue against a registry migration here, though. Migrating changes the state value for existing users from e.g. `453000` to `453`, which silently breaks any automation or template comparing the raw state, and triggers "units changed" statistics repairs on affected installs — a breaking change in exchange for a display improvement. Core pins the old unit deliberately, and the per-entity unit selector already lets existing users opt in.

@danielhiversen, happy to add a migration if you'd prefer it despite that cost — your call as code owner.

